{"base_rate":0.1098546042003231,"brier":0.07087124394184167,"bss":0.2752456309384008,"bss_hi":0.41901246651420154,"bss_lo":0.12344249352828526,"chart":{"base":[204.4,62.4],"fp":[187.3,262.1],"lead":"62,278.7 272,260.4 482,233.8 692,194.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.28 — higher than 46% of cities","fp":"low end -1pp, high end +24pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 90% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 67% → rained 45%"},"rel":"64.1,462.4 137.7,442.7 481.6,270.2"},"country":"IR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.06082390953150241,"ess":366.3415620344751,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Tehran</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Tehran rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (88%), believe about\n<b>61%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 619 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-02-27. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 9.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.28, ranked 116 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(49&ndash;167) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>361</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'><b>30%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Tehran</b> <span class=\"muted\">Iran</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.28</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>49&ndash;167\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>619 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Tehran &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Tehran\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"41